  "vendor/bb/x0x/drum808.c": {
    "commit": "c54b18d9b2389d4053375171a7497fc70418e61e",
    "path": "vendor/bb/x0x/drum808.c",
    "sha256": "d4f94223a05cbbd3881ad9af60bf39c029a57556c3fe1fc36c900803eaee3979",
    "base_sha256": "e078379b92093f716ad31dd1684838ef0cf6d854a2fa4ad58b27db0aa6559715",
    "local_change": "Compile a dry-only span for the Elite mixer from the same render loop and resolve Elite kit pots before audio publication. Elite span renderer caches phase increments between drift and jitter changes and omits the unused band-limited sum for cowbell-only spans. The span loop skips zero edge corrections, caches tail thresholds and accumulates dry samples in lane order before storing. Elite kit preparation caches the exact 808 trigger pitches. Optional PI32 RAM placement adds far calls to the two shared helpers. Elite kit preparation also resolves the six shared oscillator increments for each metal voice. Add fused mono Q23 dry output for the Elite board. Cache the two cymbal sustain resonator coefficient sets in prepared tuning. Resolve kick pitch, decay and tone coefficients at kit publication. Prepare snare and tom trigger coefficients on kit publication. Prepare rim and clap filter coefficients and the cowbell, cymbal and hat releases at kit publication. Use fixed hat filter taps and sign-bit magnitude checks in the 808 span path. Skip the pulse shaper when both the gate and history are zero. Retire choked lanes inside their gain-update branch. Use one unsigned range comparison per edge to skip zero BLEP corrections. Cache the kick output gain at the trigger. Cache the tom/conga strike gain at the trigger and refresh the resonator less often after the pitch envelope settles. Use exact weighted square values outside the metal oscillator edge windows, after Optimist e96d27bc and X0X."
  },
  "vendor/bb/x0x/drum808.h": {
    "commit": "c54b18d9b2389d4053375171a7497fc70418e61e",
    "path": "vendor/bb/x0x/drum808.h",
    "sha256": "3a3d6673ac3d746711b511db5a1c6535490fb603546a22ff96879ea46f6d70e1",
    "base_sha256": "7aa90bb7ca0468851caa2399a6946bb65ca290c4d7c4385a4f265626be6d3600",
    "local_change": "Declare the Elite dry-only span and resolve Elite kit pots before audio publication. Elite kit preparation caches the exact 808 trigger pitches. Elite kit preparation also resolves the six shared oscillator increments for each metal voice. Add fused mono Q23 dry output for the Elite board. Cache the two cymbal sustain resonator coefficient sets in prepared tuning. Resolve kick pitch, decay and tone coefficients at kit publication. Prepare snare and tom trigger coefficients on kit publication. Prepare rim and clap filter coefficients and the cowbell, cymbal and hat releases at kit publication. Store the kick output gain in the voice. Keep the tom/conga strike gain and narrower coefficient countdown in the existing footprint."
  },
